+ * memaGetLongestFree() was 259152 at that moment -- the heap was not the problem, the
+ * cached number was.
+ *
+ * bgGdlLastNeed carries the peak requirement back out so bgLoadRoomModelData can cache
+ * a size that is big enough to reload into. It is set on every path, including the
+ * refusals, so a room that failed once enlarges its own cache and recovers. */
+static s32 bgGdlLastNeed;
