+ *
+ * Retail asks `field_88C % rate == 0`, and field_88C counts TICKS. Under GETV_SIMDIV a tick
+ * is worth n fields of real time, so the rate stays constant per tick and halves per second
+ * as the divider rises. Measured on the FN P90, 240 frames of held trigger:
+ *
+ *     SIMDIV   shots/frame   shots/tick
+ *        1        0.487        0.487
+ *        2        0.250        0.500
+ *        4        0.125        0.500
+ *
+ * Constant per tick, halving per second. That is the frame-quantisation this is here to fix.
+ *
+ * field_890 is the same counter measured in FIELDS -- it accumulates g_ClockTimer and is
+ * reset at every point field_88C is -- so asking whether it crossed a multiple of the rate
+ * gives the same cadence in real time at any divider. No new state is needed: the previous
+ * value is the current one minus this tick's delta.
+ *
+ * At divider 1 g_ClockTimer is 1 per tick, so field_890 tracks field_88C exactly and the
+ * crossing test reduces to the modulo it replaces. That equivalence is verified by
+ * measurement, not assumed -- see docs/FRAME_TIMING.md.
+ *
+ * GETV_TIMEFIRE=0 restores the tick modulo for an A/B. */
