+ *
+ * A display list inside asset data is the N64's format: 8 bytes per command, two
+ * big-endian 32-bit words. Our Gfx is 16 bytes (two uintptr_t), so Fast3D reading the
+ * asset directly walks at the wrong stride -- which shows up as a stream of
