+/* GENERATED by the tvOS port - regenerate with tools/gen_monanim_index.py
+ *
+ * The monitor/TV screen bytecode is a stream of u32 words, and the original
+ * MONJUMPTO/MONJUMPCHANCE macros embedded a raw POINTER as one of those words.
+ * That is fine on the N64 where pointers are 32 bits and fatal on arm64.
+ *
+ * The word now holds an INDEX into g_MonAnimCmdlists[] instead, which keeps the
+ * stream 32-bit (the interpreter overlays struct tvcmd on it and walks it with a
+ * u16 offset, so the word size cannot change) while making the jump 64-bit clean. */
