+ *
+ * A packed font is [ s32 kerning[169] ][ fontchar[94] ][ pixel data ], all big-endian,
+ * and its fontchar records are the N64's 24 bytes -- 5x s32 plus a 4-byte pixeldata
+ * offset. Native `struct fontchar` is 32 bytes because pixeldata is a real pointer.
