+ * reinterprets individual records as ALStartParamAlt or ALStartParam depending on the
+ * message. On the N64 all three are exactly 28 bytes, so the overlay is free and
+ * invisible. At 64-bit they are not:
+ *
+ *     sizeof(ALParam)          28 -> 32
+ *     sizeof(ALStartParamAlt)  28 -> 40      <- 8 bytes larger than its own storage
+ *     sizeof(ALStartParam)     28 -> 32
