+ * `ALStartParamAlt.wave` lands at offset 32, i.e. one byte past the end of the
+ * 32-byte ALParam it is written into. alSynStartVoiceParams writes the wavetable
+ * pointer there, clobbering the next record in the pool, and alEnvmixerPull then reads
+ * `param->wave` back as NULL. That NULL reaches alLoadParam via
+ * AL_FILTER_SET_WAVETABLE, which does `a->memin = (intptr_t)a->table->base` -- and
+ * `base` is ALWaveTable's first member, so it faults at exactly address 0x0.
