+/* GETV-SFXBASE -----------------------------------------------------------------
+ * Rare's `struct ALInstrumentAlt_s` (src/snd.h) is a SECOND VIEW of the real
+ * ALInstrument, and on the N64 the view is deliberately offset by one pointer:
+ *
+ *                        N64 (4-byte ptr)        arm64 (8-byte ptr)
+ *   real  ALInstrument   soundArray @ 16         soundArray @ 16
+ *   Alt   (3 x s32)      soundArray @ 12         soundArray @ 16  (s32[3] -> pad to 16)
+ *   => Alt[k] aliases    real[k - 1]             real[k]
+ *
+ * So SFX_ID is ONE-BASED against the real soundArray -- which is why the enum
+ * opens with NOTHING_SFX == 0 and sfx.ctl's single instrument holds soundCount
+ * = 261 for an enum of 262 members, and why libultra's own __lookupSoundQuick
+ * indexes `soundArray[i - 1]` over `l = 1 .. soundCount`.
+ *
+ * On a 64-bit build the alias silently collapses and EVERY sound plays its
+ * successor (measured: arming a gun, PICKUP_GUN_SFX 232, produced
+ * PICKUP_KNIFE_SFX 233). Index 261 (BIG_CLANK_SFX) additionally runs one entry
+ * past the converted array.
